{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChDrFJ95oBngY2pUm1hv9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Change it to \"Unable to receive payment confirmation.\"** \"Recieve\" is a misspelling (\"i before e except after c\"), and a typo in a user-facing error message makes the product look careless, especially around payments.\n\nI didn't use the divergent-design process here. It only applies when there are three or more workable options with real tradeoffs, and this is a yes/no typo fix.\n\nOne thing to check before you merge: whether anything matches on the exact message text. I searched this repo for \"recieve\" and found nothing, so the string lives somewhere else (another service, a client, or config). Look in these places:\n\n- **Client code or SDKs** that compare the message string instead of an error code. If any do, fix the spelling anyway, but let those consumers know, or briefly accept both spellings.\n- **Tests, log alerts, monitoring rules or dashboards** that search for the misspelled text.\n- **Translation files**, where the English string may be used as the key.\n\nIf nothing depends on the exact wording, it's a one-line fix. If something does, that's a sign those consumers should match on a stable error code rather than the message text."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":187,"cache_read_input_tokens":4354,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":187},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93a24357-8834-4a36-88aa-8b75139a8fbd","uuid":"1bcdef74-fb9b-48de-86b3-f9d027efef4f","timestamp":"2026-11-20T08:17:22.714Z","request_id":"req_011ChDrFHuheDhtj1erLMnmu"}
